-- #1111 A-2.7: the same drain as
-- `test/llvm_fixtures_modules/ctor_scope_type_member_arity/`, enrolled HERE because
-- this corpus is the one that grades the two INTERPRETER module drivers directly:
-- `diff_compiler_eval_modules.sh` runs `eval.evalModules` (untyped) and
-- `diff_compiler_core_ir_modules.sh` runs `ir.core_ir_eval.cevalModules` over the
-- very same directory.  Those are the two parallel drivers AGENTS.md requires be
-- fixed in lockstep, and this fixture is what makes a one-sided fix red.
--
-- `import eamod.{EA(..)}` must bind eamod's `Crate` into this module's import
-- frame.  Before A-2.7 a `(..)` member bound nothing — the frame binds a member by
-- looking its ORIGIN name up in the exporting module's cells, and `EA` is a TYPE,
-- which has no cell — so `Crate` fell through to `globalCells`, which is keyed by
-- BARE name across every module's decls and holds whichever `Crate` registered
-- last.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand BEFORE any capture and independently of any
-- engine: `Crate 5` is eamod's, so `unEA (Crate 5)` = `5`; `ebv` is ebmod's
-- `Crate 8 2` and `unEB (Crate a b) = a - b` = `8 - 2` = `6`.  So `5` then `6`.
--
-- ⚠️ Measured on pristine `main` `ae39ec41`, BOTH drivers died
-- `E-NONEXHAUSTIVE-MATCH` on this program while `medaka build` printed the right
-- answers — the eval-vs-native divergence A-2.7 closes.
import eamod.{EA(..), unEA}
import ebmod.{EB, ebv, unEB}

main =
  println (unEA (Crate 5))
  println (unEB ebv)
